      formula: "Framework: compare cases by grouping internal and external causes of decline.",
      substitution: "Each state had internal weaknesses such as poor leadership or corruption, and each faced a stronger external enemy.",
      calculation: "In all three cases internal decline left the state vulnerable to outside attack.",
      answer: "A common pattern is that internal weakness left each empire open to defeat by an outside power."
